# **3. Cooling system**

## **3.1 Peltier module**

The selected cooling load discussed so far is:

# **12 V · 6 A**

**Peltier module maximum electrical load**

# **72 W**

\\[ P=V\times I=12\times6=72\text{ W} \\]

The Peltier module works using the thermoelectric effect. When DC power is applied, one side becomes cold and the other side becomes hot.

The hot side must continuously release the heat it receives from the cold side, plus the electrical energy consumed by the Peltier module.

This makes hot-side heat dissipation extremely important.

## **3.2 Cooling arrangement**

The design direction discussed was to place the Peltier assembly on the side of the medicine chamber rather than underneath it.

The intended arrangement is:

- Peltier module mounted on the side wall.
- Hot-side heatsink and fan placed outside the chamber.
- Cold-side heatsink placed inside the chamber.
- A small internal fan to circulate cold air inside the medicine chamber.
- Hot-side air intake and outlet arranged to maintain proper airflow.

